* bench_opamp_macro: supply-powered voltage-feedback op-amp macromodel (project-authored, textbook topology).
* Ports: inp inn vcc vee out.  Built only from R, C, V, I, D and linear E/G sources.
* Stage 1: transconductance G1 into R1, clamped to +-10 V by near-ideal diodes (the input stage's limited
*   linear range). Stage 2: G2 charges C2: the clamp caps the charging current, so the slew rate is SR exactly:
*   SR = G2 * 10 V / C2.  Small-signal: unity-gain frequency GBW = G1*R1*G2 / (2 pi C2); R2 sets the DC gain AOL.
* The integrator node n2 is clamped between (vee + VDROPL) and (vcc - VDROPH): the output swing limits.
* Eout buffers n2 through ROUT. Internal nodes are referenced to node 0, so output current is supplied from ground,
* not from vcc/vee; the supply pins draw the constant quiescent current IQ and the clamp currents only.
* AOL: DC open-loop gain (V/V). GBW (Hz). SR (V/s). VOS: input offset (V, added to the + input). IB: bias current
* into each input (A; negative = out of the pin, as for PNP inputs). ROUT (ohm). IQ: supply current (A).
* VDROPH / VDROPL: output headroom to the positive / negative rail (V).
.subckt bench_opamp_macro inp inn vcc vee out params: AOL=100k GBW=1meg SR=0.5meg VOS=0 IB=0 ROUT=50 IQ=1m
+ VDROPH=1.5 VDROPL=1.5
.model bench_dclamp D(Is=1e-15 N=0.01)
Rinp inp 0 1e12
Rinn inn 0 1e12
Ibp inp 0 DC {IB}
Ibn inn 0 DC {IB}
Vos ip inp DC {VOS}
Iq vcc vee DC {IQ}
* stage 1: v(n1) = 1meg * G1 * vd, clamped to +-10 V. C1 adds a pole at 100 x GBW (0.6 degree of phase): without
* it the algebraic stage 1 plus the sharp clamps rang numerically at time steps near 1 / GBW.
G1 0 n1 ip inn {6.283185307179586*GBW*10/SR/1meg}
R1 n1 0 1meg
C1 n1 0 {1/(6.283185307179586*100*GBW*1meg)}
Vcp cp 0 DC 10
Vcn 0 cn DC 10
D1 n1 cp bench_dclamp
D2 cn n1 bench_dclamp
* stage 2: integrator, C2 = 1 nF, G2 = SR * C2 / 10 V
G2 0 n2 n1 0 {SR*1e-10}
C2 n2 0 1n
R2 n2 0 {AOL/(6.283185307179586*GBW*1n)}
* rails: each clamp source is widened by the clamp diode's drop at the full integrator current SR * 1 nF / 1 V,
* so a saturated output sits exactly VDROPH / VDROPL inside the rail (before ROUT)
Ehi hi1 0 vcc 0 1
Vhi hi1 hi DC {VDROPH+0.01*0.025865*ln(SR*1e-9/1e-15)}
Elo lo1 0 vee 0 1
Vlo lo lo1 DC {VDROPL+0.01*0.025865*ln(SR*1e-9/1e-15)}
D3 n2 hi bench_dclamp
D4 lo n2 bench_dclamp
* output
Eout ob 0 n2 0 1
Rout ob out {ROUT}
.ends bench_opamp_macro
